.TH "PB-CONFIG-CONFLICT-RESOLVE" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-config-conflict-resolve - Choose the machine or repository version


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb config conflict resolve <environment> <path> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Choose the machine or repository version

.PP
Resolve one exact path with --keep to select the machine or repository version. Use show first to inspect both sides; the chosen direction is recorded for synchronization.

.PP
Conflicts identify exact paths whose local and repository versions cannot be merged automatically. Review the affected path before choosing a side; resolution records a deliberate decision for the next synchronization step.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for resolve

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--keep\fP=""
	version to keep: machine or repository


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-config-conflict(1)\fP
